From: cyprox <enrk@kaspa.network>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: bind each oracle output to its own authorizing input

The committed harness binds every output to authorizing input 0. The
generated `PriceRound::use` requires each input to authorize exactly one
output, so `OpAuthOutputCount(0)` returns N instead of 1 and the ladder
fails at N = 2 with "input 0 script failed: script ran, but verification
failed".

This check is present verbatim in the .sil fixtures committed at Argent
d08e52d, so the committed harness could never have produced the published
ladder on either revision. The working copy that produced it was not the
copy that was committed.

crates/argent-runtime/src/resolve.rs binds outputs to distinct authorizing
inputs within a single transaction, so per-input binding is intended usage.
CovenantBinding::new takes a u16 (consensus/core/src/tx.rs).

With this applied, both variants validate the full ladder to N = 512 and
reproduce every published figure to the unit.

--- a/tests/enrk_mass.rs
+++ b/tests/enrk_mass.rs
@@
-        for _ in 0..n {
-            context = context.actor_output("PriceRound", state.clone(), CovenantBinding::new(0, covenant_id), UTXO_VALUE);
-        }
+        for index in 0..n {
+            context = context.actor_output("PriceRound", state.clone(), CovenantBinding::new(index as u16, covenant_id), UTXO_VALUE);
+        }
